WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.866
Randomness is about uncertainty.

2
00:00:01.866 --> 00:00:10.361
Pseudorandomness comes from deterministic algorithms that produce output
that may look random, but is generated from internal state and sometimes a
seed.

3
00:00:10.361 --> 00:00:16.667
Deterministic pseudorandom output can be useful for repeatable tests,
simulations, and controlled experiments.

4
00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:21.880
It is dangerous for secrets when the seed or internal state can be known,
guessed, or influenced.

5
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.612
Entropy is unpredictability available to the system at a high level.

6
00:00:25.612 --> 00:00:33.077
Operating systems collect uncertainty from multiple sources and provide
randomness facilities intended for security-sensitive use.

7
00:00:33.077 --> 00:00:42.537
Cryptographically secure pseudorandom number generators take that entropy
and produce values suitable for keys, tokens, and other security purposes
when used correctly.

8
00:00:42.537 --> 00:00:47.557
Developers do not usually need to build these systems; they need to call
the right interface.

9
00:00:47.557 --> 00:00:51.547
Repeatability is a feature in tests and a liability in secret generation.

10
00:00:51.547 --> 00:00:57.853
A deterministic seed can make a sequence of values repeat, which is
excellent when a unit test needs stable behavior.

11
00:00:57.853 --> 00:01:04.546
The same repeatability is unacceptable for password reset tokens, session
identifiers, API keys, or cryptographic keys.

12
00:01:04.546 --> 00:01:09.694
Production security should not depend on test seeds, sample values, or
predictable defaults.

13
00:01:09.694 --> 00:01:15.164
The security question is not whether a value looks random in a log or
seems hard for a human to remember.

14
00:01:15.164 --> 00:01:23.208
The question is whether an attacker with knowledge of the application,
timing, environment, and generation method can predict or search the
value.

15
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:29.000
Secure randomness assumes the design may be inspected and still requires
values to remain unpredictable.
